transcript.text:
Here's the full workflow — create the transform, then preview it against a real identity before touching any profile.

---

## Step 1 — Obtain a token

Your PAT needs both scopes. Request them together:

```bash
TOKEN=$(curl -s -X POST "https://{tenant}.api.identitynow.com/oauth/token" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "grant_type": "client_credentials",
    "client_id":     "YOUR_CLIENT_ID",
    "client_secret": "YOUR_CLIENT_SECRET"
  }' | jq -r '.access_token')
```

---

## Step 2 — Create the transform

I'll show two common patterns. Pick one (or both).

### Option A — `upper` (uppercase a source attribute)

```bash
curl -s -X POST "https://{tenant}.api.identitynow.com/v3/transforms" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "name": "upper-firstname",
    "type": "upper",
    "attributes": {
      "input": {
        "type": "accountAttribute",
        "attributes": {
          "sourceName": "Active Directory",
          "attributeName": "givenName"
        }
      }
    }
  }' | jq .
```

### Option B — `concat` (build a dotted username)

```bash
curl -s -X POST "https://{tenant}.api.identitynow.com/v3/transforms" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "name": "concat-dot-username",
    "type": "concat",
    "attributes": {
      "values": [
        {
          "type": "accountAttribute",
          "attributes": {
            "sourceName": "Active Directory",
            "attributeName": "givenName"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "static",
          "attributes": { "value": "." }
        },
        {
          "type": "accountAttribute",
          "attributes": {
            "sourceName": "Active Directory",
            "attributeName": "sn"
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  }' | jq .
```

The response will include an `id` field — the transform is now saved and addressable by name.

---

## Step 3 — Test with the identity preview endpoint

This endpoint runs the transform against a real identity **without persisting anything** — ideal for validation before wiring into a profile.

You need an `identityId` (grab one from `GET /v3/identities` or the UI). Replace `uid` below with whichever identity attribute you want to preview the transform on.

```bash
curl -s -X POST "https://{tenant}.api.identitynow.com/beta/identity-profiles/identity-preview" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -H "X-SailPoint-Experimental: true" \
  -d '{
    "identityId": "2c9180857182305e0171993735622948",
    "identityAttributeConfig": {
      "enabled": true,
      "attributeTransforms": [
        {
          "identityAttributeName": "uid",
          "transformDefinition": {
            "type": "reference",
            "attributes": {
              "id": "concat-dot-username"
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  }' | jq '.previewAttributes[] | select(.name == "uid")'
```

The `type: "reference"` + `id: "<transform-name>"` tells the preview engine to resolve the transform you just created. The filtered response will show you the computed value for that identity before you commit it to a profile mapping.

**Key notes:**
- `X-SailPoint-Experimental: true` is required — the preview endpoint is beta-only.
- `identityAttributeName` must match a valid attribute name in your identity schema.
- You can test multiple attributes in a single call by adding more entries to `attributeTransforms`.
- To inline-test (without a saved transform), replace `type: "reference"` with the full transform definition object directly in `transformDefinition`.

---

## Scopes summary

| Step | Scope required |
|------|---------------|
| Create transform | `idn:transform:manage` |
| Preview | `idn:identity-profile:manage` |

---

```answer-summary
endpoints:
  - method: POST
    path: /v3/transforms
    api_version: v3
  - method: POST
    path: /beta/identity-profiles/identity-preview
    api_version: beta
auth_flow: OAuth2 bearer token
required_scopes: [idn:transform:manage, idn:identity-profile:manage]
key_parameters: [name, type, attributes, identityId, identityAttributeConfig, identityAttributeName, transformDefinition]
```

